# Unit Testing

All unit tests use Swift Testing and mirror the relative folder structure of the code under test.

## Swift Testing

- Use [Swift Testing](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/testing) (`import Testing`), not XCTest.
- Use `@Test`, `#expect`, and `@Suite` where appropriate.
- Name test types `{TypeUnderTest}Tests` (e.g. `CoastingModelTests`).

```swift
import Testing
@testable import CSCSEmulator

@Suite struct TypeUnderTestTests {
    @Test func describesExpectedBehavior() {
        let result = TypeUnderTest().performAction()
        #expect(result == .expectedValue)
    }
}
```

## Mirrored Folder Structure

- Test target root: `CSCSEmulatorTests/`
- Preserve the subdirectory path under `CSCSEmulator/` (drop only the `CSCSEmulator/` prefix).
- Prefer one mirrored test file per primary source type; append `Tests` to the filename.
- When adding, moving, or renaming source files, apply the same change to the mirrored test path.

Examples:

- `CSCSEmulator/Simulation/CoastingModel.swift` -> `CSCSEmulatorTests/Simulation/CoastingModelTests.swift`
- `CSCSEmulator/BLE/CSCSMeasurementEncoder.swift` -> `CSCSEmulatorTests/BLE/CSCSMeasurementEncoderTests.swift`
- `CSCSEmulator/ViewModels/RunningViewModel.swift` -> `CSCSEmulatorTests/ViewModels/RunningViewModelTests.swift`

`App/` and pure SwiftUI `Views/` may have little unit-test coverage; mirror structure when tests are added (e.g. ViewModel tests under `ViewModels/`, not `Views/`).

## Tests With Functional Changes

- Any change that adds, removes, or changes behavior must include corresponding unit test additions, removals, or updates in the mirrored test file.
- Exemptions: documentation-only, assets, or project config with no behavior change; pure refactors that do not alter observable behavior (existing tests must still pass).
- If a functional change does not update tests, the final summary must explicitly state why tests were not applicable.
- Treat missing or outdated tests as incomplete work.

See [`.cursor/rules/dependency-injection.mdc`](.cursor/rules/dependency-injection.mdc) for testability conventions (protocols, constructor injection).
